<!-- What is Geographic Targeting Section -->
<section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="content-block">
            <h2>What is Geographic Targeting?</h2>
            <p>Geographic targeting focuses on improving visibility for searches with local intent. When someone searches for "pipefitter near me" or "cafe in Surry Hills," geographic work determines which businesses appear in those results.</p>
            <p>Geographic results differ from standard organic results. They include map listings, business information panels, and results weighted toward proximity to the searcher.</p>
            <p>For businesses that serve specific geographic areas, this type of work is often more relevant than broader organic optimisation because it connects you with people actively looking for services in your location.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- How It Works Section -->
<section class="content-section alt-bg">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="content-block">
            <h2>How Geographic Visibility Works</h2>
            <p>Geographic ranking depends on three primary factors:</p>
            <ul class="content-list">
                <li><strong>Relevance:</strong> How well your business matches what the searcher is looking for</li>
                <li><strong>Distance:</strong> How close your business is to the searcher or the location in their search</li>
                <li><strong>Prominence:</strong> How well-known and authoritative your business appears online</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Geographic work addresses all three factors through business listing optimisation, citation building, review management and content development.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

